Z||000013||MinnGreenGT||09-13-2001||09:37 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by BlackDragon:<BR><B>i agree, i like the rectangle lights better, but the plexiglass is definitely a good thing too. i wonder if you could get just the plexi glass peice from somewhere.... maybe the guy that makes the rectangle lights cold make it<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I believe that Darrell Morse (known for Bored TB/Plenums & Strut Tower Braces) Made a set for Kevin Lindeman (KEV) awhile ago- he's using Tom's kit too.  I haven't seen his car since he had them done- next time I see him I'll check them out!<P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngtsig3.jpg">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/halfpole.gif">  <BR>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett||||reg||1
Z||000014||chester||09-14-2001||02:08 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by tomanyfieros:<BR><B>chester, where did u get those rims? i love those, i would be thinking of getting those and putting them on my (hopefully future fiero) ttop 88 coupe.... LMK<BR>Thanx Jason<BR>also, does anyone have those flushmount headlites sitting around that they want to sell? <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Thanks, I got the rims from an outlet in Texas I think.  I'll look it up and get back to you.  Took me 4 months of web browsing to finally settle on these.  I love the look.<P>Rob D.<p>[This message has been edited by chester (edited 09-14-2001).]||||reg||1
