Z||000018||rogergarrison||09-14-2001||07:14 PM||||I built mine up from scratch. Dont use plexiglass, use Lexan. It almost unbreakable. Believe it or not, the covers are held on by Velcro on all four corners so no attaching screws show. I also ran a rubber seal all along the edge underneath to help keep water and dirt out. They havent blown off up to 150 mph yet. the only problem ive had was last winter i got caught out in an ice storm and they iced over, had to use my lower driving lites. (but then again, you could just take the covers off in a few seconds) <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/P1000576.jpg[/img][img]http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/P1000577.jpg"> <p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 09-14-2001).]||||reg||1
